"1.1.21": {"q": "Certificate of Insurance in respect of Wreck Removal Issued by : ____", "cat": "S", "gp": "I", "p": 25, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "Bunker Convention", "The Bunkers Convention requires the owners of vessels over 1000 GT registered in a state party to the Convention to maintain compulsory insurance to cover liability for pollution damage (including the costs of preventative measures) caused in the territorial sea of a State Party, as well as in its exclusive economic zone, or equivalent area. Dry Bulk vessels do not require a CLC for Oil Pollution."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.22": {"q": "USCG Certificate of Compliance", "cat": "NS", "gp": "SI", "p": 25, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "Information only", "This question should be answered to identify if the ship has a valid USCG Certificate of Compliance. This question is for information only and is non-scoring. A Certificate of Compliance can only be obtained after USCG inspection. To be answered Yes, the Certificate of Compliance must have been issued within the last two years. Any limitations or outstanding deficiencies noted in the CoC should be recorded in the remarks. Not applicable for dry bulk vessels."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.23": {"q": "USCG Certificate of Financial Responsibility (Water Pollution)", "cat": "NS", "gp": "SI", "p": 25, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "Information only", "This certificate is not issued anymore in hard copy, but is available online. If a valid print-out or online version is shown, answer in the affirmative."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.24": {"q": "P & I Certificate of Entry", "cat": "R", "gp": "I", "p": 25, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "", "Some clubs (Gard for e.g..) do not issue hard copy of P & I Club Certificate but soft copy only. Soft copies are acceptable."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.25": {"q": "Name of Club", "cat": "", "gp": "I", "p": 25, "b": "Core", "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.26": {"q": "Minimum Safe Manning Document (or equivalent)", "cat": "S", "gp": "I", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "SOLAS IMO A", "The manning level onboard must be appropriate based on whether it is operating UMS or not. Also, if the manning level is specific to the trade/trading area, the vessel must be in compliance."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.27": {"q": "A record of lifting appliances (or equivalent as per flag requirements) is completed correctly and up to date", "cat": "S", "gp": "SI", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "ILO COSWP", "This record should detail the examination and testing of all lifting appliances on board, including engine room cranes, deck cranes, derricks, etc. The document may take different formats including loose leaf form. ILO 162 Art.22 states that every lifting appliance item of loose gear shall be tested in accordance with National laws before being put into use for the first time. Lifting gear forming part of a ship's equipment shall be retested once every five years. Art.23 states that lifting appliances and loose gear shall be thoroughly examined and certified by a competent person at least once every 12 months."]], "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.28": {"q": "Copy of Document of Compliance", "cat": "S", "gp": "I", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.29": {"q": "Issued by: ____", "cat": "", "gp": "I", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.30": {"q": "Safety Management Certificate", "cat": "S", "gp": "I", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "see": "1.1.1"},
"1.1.31": {"q": "Issued by: ____", "cat": "", "gp": "I", "p": 26, "b": "Core", "see": "1.1.1"},
