"1.1.42": {"q": "All deficiencies from last Port State Control inspections have been closed out and if No, list the outstanding deficiencies.", "cat": "D", "gp": "I", "p": 27, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "", "May be N/A only for vessels that have not had any deficiencies on their last Port State Control inspection, or for new vessels that have not yet undergone their first Port State Control inspection. If No, list the outstanding deficiencies."]]},
"1.1.43": {"q": "The vessel has not been detained as a result of Port State inspection in the last 36 months under the present management, and if No, list detention details (port state authority, etc.) and deficiencies that led to detention.", "cat": "D", "gp": "I", "p": 27, "b": "Core"},
"1.1.44": {"q": "The on-line VPQ (dry bulk) or HVPQ (tankers) appears up-to- date and accurately completed", "cat": "R", "gp": "I", "p": 27, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "", "The VPQ/HVPQ should be kept updated in the on-line CDI database, and it is not required to provide a printed copy for the purpose of the CDI inspection. The inspector should download the VPQ/HVPQ before boarding and verify the accuracy of the variable data, with a particular attention for the chapters 1, 2 & 3."]]},
