"1.2.32": {"q": "The latest editions of the following publications are on-board when required:", "cat": "R", "gp": "SI", "p": 30, "b": "Core", "g": [["", "OCIMF/ICS ICS ICS SIGTTO OCIMF ICS NI OCIMF/ICS ICS CDI / OCIMF / ICS / SIGTTO OCIMF OCIMF BA BA BA IALA SIGTTO SIGTTO", "Inspectors should spot check the library on the vessel to ensure that the vessel has the latest edition and amendments of all appropriate publications, which should include: (list publication and edition or other appropriate detail, and incorporate following guidance notes when appropriate).\n-International Safety Guide for Oil Tankers and Terminals (ISGOTT) - for tankers\n-Tanker Safety Guide (Chemicals)\n-Tanker Safety Guide (Liquefied Gas)\n-Liquefied Gas Handling Principles on Ships and in Terminals\n-Guidelines for the Control of Drugs and Alcohol On board Ship\n-Bridge Procedures Guide\n-Bridge Team Management\n-Best Management Practices to Deter Piracy\n-ICS Guide to Helicopter / Ship Operations\n-Ship to Ship Transfer Guide for Petroleum, Chemicals and Liquefied Gases (only for tankers)\n-Effective Mooring\n-Mooring Equipment Guidelines (only for tankers)\n-Admiralty Guide to the Practical Use of ENCs (NP231)\n-Admiralty Guide to ENC Symbols Used in ECDIS (NP5012)\n-Admiralty Guide to ECDIS Implementation, Policy and Procedures (NP232)\n-I.A.L.A. Buoyage Systems (Admiralty NP 735)\n-ESD Systems 2.1 (LPG carriers)\n-Liquefied Petroleum Gas Sampling Procedures (for LPG tankers)\n-Any other document as required in the vessel's SMS Plan"]]},
